             magnitude as fresh-vs-frozen. So the frozen per-example values were never
             reproducible against any other draw. The pipeline IS deterministic given a
             fixed list, order and batch size. The live-vs-frozen source plays no part.
             NOTHING REPORTED CHANGES. The Tier used the frozen CSVs; the primary
             contrast pairs clean HARM against clean ISO on the same list, hence the
             same batches and seeds, i.e. common random numbers. The cross-protocol DiD
             pairs frozen leaky draws against fresh clean ones and so carries an
             unpaired-draw noise term the example-level bootstrap does not model; it was
             already diagnostic-only and was not recomputed.
             Corrections made: RESULT.md's "and/or the live-vs-frozen source" hedge
             replaced by the diagnosis; REPRODUCIBILITY.md gains section 3 item 0 stating
             that per-example values are specific to the list, its order and the batch
             size, and the float32-reduction paragraph now points at it.
